  "approach": {
    "title": "Proof of Continuity Using the Epsilon-Delta Definition",
    "preliminaries": {
      "definition": "A function f is continuous at a point x = a if for every ε > 0, there exists a δ > 0 such that |f(x) - f(a)| < ε whenever |x - a| < δ.",
      "goal": "Show that for every ε > 0, there exists δ > 0 such that |f(x) - f(2)| < ε whenever |x - 2| < δ."
    },
    "step_1_evaluate_function_at_point": {
      "description": "Compute f(2) to determine the target value.",
      "computation": "f(2) = (2)^3 - 3(2) + 1 = 8 - 6 + 1 = 3",
      "result": "f(2) = 3"
    },
    "step_2_set_up_the_expression": {
      "description": "Compute |f(x) - f(2)| and factor it.",
      "computation": [
        "|f(x) - f(2)| = |(x^3 - 3x + 1) - 3|",
        "= |x^3 - 3x - 2|",
        "= |(x - 2)(x^2 + 2x + 1)|",
        "= |x - 2| * |x + 1|^2"
      ],
      "note": "The polynomial x^3 - 3x - 2 factors as (x - 2)(x^2 + 2x + 1)."
    },
    "step_3_bound_the_factor": {
      "description": "Restrict δ to control the size of |x + 1|^2.",
      "assumption": "Let δ ≤ 1. Then |x - 2| < 1 implies 1 < x < 3.",
      "consequence": "Hence 2 < x + 1 < 4, so |x + 1| < 4, giving |x + 1|^2 < 16.",
      "bound": "|f(x) - f(2)| = |x - 2| * |x + 1|^2 < 16 * |x - 2|"
    },
    "step_4_choose_delta": {
      "description": "Select δ to guarantee the inequality |f(x) - f(2)| < ε.",
      "choice": "δ = min(1, ε / 16)"
    },
    "step_5_verify": {
      "description": "Confirm that the chosen δ works.",
      "argument": "Suppose |x - 2| < δ. Then since δ ≤ 1, we have |x + 1|^2 < 16, and since δ ≤ ε/16, we have |x - 2| < ε/16. Therefore: |f(x) - f(2)| < 16 * |x - 2| < 16 * (ε/16) = ε."
    },
    "conclusion": "For every ε > 0, we have found δ = min(1, ε/16) such that |x - 2| < δ implies |f(x) - f(2)| < ε. Hence, by definition, f(x) = x^3 - 3x + 1 is continuous at x = 2."
